==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkuːpə(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cooper.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːpə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{suffix|en|coop|er}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}
{{wikipedia|Cooper (profession)}}

# A [[craftsman]] who makes and repairs [[barrel]]s and similar [[wooden]] [[vessel]]s such as [[cask]]s, [[bucket]]s and [[tub]]s.
#*{{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|chapter=5|passage=They were nearly all whalemen; chief mates, and second mates, and third mates, and sea carpenters, and sea '''coopers''', and sea blacksmiths, and harpooneers, and ship keepers; a brown and brawny company, with bosky beards; an unshorn, shaggy set, all wearing monkey jackets for morning gowns.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A drink of half [[stout]] and half [[porter]].

